 - **Musketmen — AI role**: now also flagged with `UNITAI_ATTACK_CITY`, so the AI uses Musketmen more often in **offensive city-assault** roles. Civ-specific Musketman variants may also include additional changes.
 - **Grenadiers & Bazookas — AI role**: now also flagged with `UNITAI_CITY_DEFENSE`, so the AI may use them more for **city defense**.
 - **War target selection — distance guard**: added a **distance-based pre-filter** in `Risk::preEvaluate` (WarUtilityAspect.cpp) so the AI **rejects faraway rivals** during war-risk evaluation. This curbs “bait” wars that leave cores under-defended and keeps armies concentrated near relevant fronts. See [KI#61](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#61---seemingly-tremendously-improved-ais-getting-baited-to-attack-faraway-rivals-leaving-their-core-cities-mostly-defenseless-but-anyways-etc-and-oftentimes-dying-shortly-after-to-an-opportunistic-rivals-changed-by-adding-a-pre-filter-reject-in-war-risk-assessment-based-on-distance-to-us-in-riskpreevaluate-in-warutilityaspectcpp).
-- **City evacuation — doomed city auto-retreat (land units only)**: in `CvUnitAI::AI_evacuateCity`, the AI now **evacuates 100% of its land units** from a **doomed city**. Previously it often retreated only a tiny fraction (e.g., 2 of 11 defenders vs a 22+ stack, whereas now all 11 defenders would evacuate if the city is deemed doomed). This change might prolong wars/game length (although it is not tested beyond the sample case to know for sure if it would be so), but the intent is a **more competitive, less self-sabotaging** AI. See [KI#62](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#62---extremely-betterstronger-ai-almost-not-evacuating-at-all-doomed-cities-2-swordsmen-in-an-11-unit-defending-stack-vs-a-22-attacking-unit-stack-fixed-by-always-and-100-retreat-regardless-of-land-unit-type-in-cvunitaiai_evacuatecity).
+- **City evacuation — doomed city auto-retreat (land units only)**: in `CvUnitAI::AI_evacuateCity`, the AI now **evacuates 100% of its land units** from a **doomed city**. Previously it often retreated only a tiny fraction (e.g., 2 of 11 defenders vs a 22+ stack, whereas now all 11 defenders would evacuate if the city is deemed doomed). This change might prolong wars/game length (although it is not tested beyond the sample case to know for sure if it would be so), but the intent is a **more competitive, less self-sabotaging** AI. See [KI#62](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#62---extremely-betterstronger-ai-almost-not-evacuating-at-all-doomed-cities-2-swordsmen-in-an-11-unit-defending-stack-vs-a-22-attacking-unit-stack-fixed-by-always-and-100-evacuating-city-doomed-city-regardless-of-land-unit-type-in-cvunitaiai_evacuatecity).
 - **City attack oscillation — pre-check vs strong targets (needs more testing)**: In `CvUnitAI::AI_attackCityMove`, add a sanity check to **skip marching to/attacking a city** when the **defending stack is too strong**. Intended to prevent the inefficient **advance → abort → backtrack** loop and reduce the risk of being caught unable to retreat in time. Note: this oscillation sometimes resolved after ~2+ autoplay turns even without the change, so treat this as a **possible fix/mitigation** pending further testing.
 - **City attack oscillation — pre-check vs strong targets (possible mitigation)**: In `CvUnitAI::AI_attackCityMove`, add a sanity check to **skip marching to/attacking a city** when the **defending stack is too strong**. Goal: prevent the inefficient **advance → abort → backtrack** loop and reduce the risk of being caught without time to retreat. **Note:** in the test sample, this behavior also resolved without the change by running ~2+ autoplay turns in a row instead of 1 turn only from a slightly older save file rather; treat this as a **possible fix/sanity check** (not (at least not yet) broadly tested). See [KI#63](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#63---possibly-prevented-and-possibly-fixed-weird--very-inefficient-back-and-forth-of-going-to-attack-a-city-stack-and-then-going-back-after-seeing-enemy-stack-is-too-strong-i-dont-know-if-this-change-fixes-it-since-the-issue-was-solved-without-it-2-autoplay-turns-were-needed-at-least-it-seems-not-1-but-maybe-this-change-in-cvunitaiai_attackcitymove-helps-a-lot-but-anyways-etc).
+- **Early-game razing — distance-aware captures**: Updated conquer/raze logic so that, for roughly the first **~120 turns** (scaled by game speed), the AI **razes captured cities** that aren’t **close enough** to justify early investment. This addresses the base AdvCiv pattern where forces overextend (most troops sit in a faraway capture while **core cities** thin out) and also preserves scarce early economy (city maintenance, low pop, time to build improvements/culture). Indirect effect: less fog-busting far from us → **more barbarians** there, which tends to pressure rivals. Net: a **stronger, more focused** early AI (fewer “split in two” empires). See [KI#64](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#64---greatly-enhanced-ai-not-razing-faraway-cities-at-captures---now-we-raze-them-if-we-are-in-the-early-game-and-they-are-not-close-enough-thanks-to-changes-and-tweaks-in-cvplayeraiai_conquercity-anyways-etc).
 
